surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Revised recommendations for HIV testing of adults, adolescents, and pregnant women in health-care settings</article-title><source>MMWR Recomm Rep</source><year>2006</year><volume>55</volume><issue>RR-14</issue><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16988643</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Curry</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunungam</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Annerud</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>HIV antibody seroprevalence in the emergency department at Port Moresby General Hospital, Papua New Guinea</article-title><source>Emerg Med Australas</source><year>2005</year><volume>17</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>359</fpage><lpage>362</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1742-6723.2005.00757.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16091098</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakanjako</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamya</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Daniel</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Acceptance of routine testing for HIV among adult patients at the medical emergency unit at a national referral hospital in Kampala, Uganda</article-title><source>AIDS Behav</source><year>2007</year><volume>11</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>753</fpage><lpage>758</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10461-006-9180-9</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17096199</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waxman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimaiyo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ongaro</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Initial outcomes of an emergency department rapid HIV testing program in western Kenya</article-title><source>AIDS Patient Care STDS</source><year>2007</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>981</fpage><lpage>986</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/apc.2007.0075</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18154494</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Waxman M, Kimaiyo W, Wandabwa M et al (2006) Diagnostic testing and counseling (DTC) at Moi Teaching and Referral Hospital (MTRH): a summary of the first years experience (abstract). Kenyan Medical Association pre-conference, Eldoret, Kenya, March 2006</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wools-Kaloustian</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimaiyo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Diero</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Viability and effectiveness of large-scale HIV treatment initiatives in sub-Saharan Africa: experience from western Kenya</article-title><source>AIDS</source><year>2006</year><volume>20</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.aids.0000196177.65551.ea</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16327318</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">National AIDS and STD Control Programme (2004) Guidelines for HIV testing in clinical settings. Ministry of Health, Republic of Kenya</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">UNAIDS/WHO (2007) Guidance on provider-initiated HIV testing and counseling in health facilities. UNAIDS/WHO, Geneva</mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>